							},
							{
								"key": 515,
								"value": [
									"sfizz~ @pathmode 3 @volume -18",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @pathmode   ·   entry 515",
									"VALUES: int; 0–4; default 0; alias defaultpathmode\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)",
									"Chooses how dictionary sample paths are resolved.",
									"Dictionary input only. Modes: 0 search path; 1 Max Library; 2 last SFZ folder; 3 patcher folder; 4 dictionary default_path. For mode 3, save the patch and place the real sample beside it. Use sfizz~ Help’s dictionary structure; regular SFZ files retain their own relative-path rules.",
									"// MAX OBJECT ATTRIBUTE: pathmode\n// Create this Max object: sfizz~ @pathmode 3 @volume -18\n// MAX inlet message: pathmode 3\n// Then send the dictionary from the Dictionaries tab of sfizz~ Help.\n// The SFZ below is a separate baseline playback check.\n// Save the SFZ below; load it using read. Max settings above are comments only.\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_SAMPLE.wav key=60 loop_mode=one_shot\nvolume=-18\n",
									"Send a dictionary referencing a sample basename. In mode 3, verify playback from the saved patcher folder. Changing pathmode on an ordinary loaded .sfz file is not an audible test.",
									"Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @pathmode   ·   entry 515\nVALUES: int; 0–4; default 0; alias defaultpathmode\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)\nWHAT: Chooses how dictionary sample paths are resolved.\nREQUIRES: Dictionary input only. Modes: 0 search path; 1 Max Library; 2 last SFZ folder; 3 patcher folder; 4 dictionary default_path. For mode 3, save the patch and place the real sample beside it. Use sfizz~ Help’s dictionary structure; regular SFZ files retain their own relative-path rules.\nTRY: Send a dictionary referencing a sample basename. In mode 3, verify playback from the saved patcher folder. Changing pathmode on an ordinary loaded .sfz file is not an audible test.\nBUILD NOTE: Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.\nSOURCE: https://docs.cycling74.com/reference/sfizz~/"
								]
							},
							{
								"key": 516,
								"value": [
									"sfizz~ @ref 60 @base 440. @volume -18",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @ref   ·   entry 516",
									"VALUES: int; MIDI reference note; default 69\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)",
									"Assigns the reference frequency to a MIDI note.",
									"Use base together with ref and a pitched source. For a simple comparison, use a fresh object with default tuning and no external keyboard map. Keep SFZ transpose/tune unchanged.",
									"// MAX OBJECT ATTRIBUTE: ref\n// Create this Max object: sfizz~ @ref 60 @base 440. @volume -18\n// MAX messages: base 440.; ref 69; later ref 60\n// Restore ref 69 after the comparison.\n// Save the SFZ below; load it using read. Max settings above are comments only.\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=0 hikey=127 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-12 ampeg_attack=0.01 ampeg_release=0.25\n",
									"With base 440., compare the same played note using ref 69 and ref 60. Use a tuner and replay the note after each change to observe the shifted reference.",
									"Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @ref   ·   entry 516\nVALUES: int; MIDI reference note; default 69\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)\nWHAT: Assigns the reference frequency to a MIDI note.\nREQUIRES: Use base together with ref and a pitched source. For a simple comparison, use a fresh object with default tuning and no external keyboard map. Keep SFZ transpose/tune unchanged.\nTRY: With base 440., compare the same played note using ref 69 and ref 60. Use a tuner and replay the note after each change to observe the shifted reference.\nBUILD NOTE: Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.\nSOURCE: https://docs.cycling74.com/reference/sfizz~/"
								]
							},
							{
								"key": 517,
								"value": [
									"sfizz~ @scale 6 200.0 400.0 600.0 800.0 1000.0 1200.0 @volume -18",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @scale   ·   entry 517",
									"VALUES: atom list; note count followed by cents or ratios\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)",
									"Defines Scala tuning intervals directly as a list.",
									"Use pitched notes and pitch tracking. The example has six intervals per octave. Decimal values are cents; ratios use a slash. The 0-cent root is implicit, so omit it from the list. Keep an explicit keyboard map out of this first test.",
									"// MAX OBJECT ATTRIBUTE: scale\n// Create this Max object: sfizz~ @scale 6 200.0 400.0 600.0 800.0 1000.0 1200.0 @volume -18\n// MAX whole-tone: scale 6 200.0 400.0 600.0 800.0 1000.0 1200.0\n// MAX 12-tone equal temperament: scale 12 100.0 200.0 300.0 400.0 500.0 600.0 700.0 800.0 900.0 1000.0 1100.0 1200.0\n// Save the SFZ below; load it using read. Max settings above are comments only.\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=0 hikey=127 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-12 ampeg_attack=0.01 ampeg_release=0.25\n",
									"Load the sine example and play successive MIDI keys. Compare the six-note whole-tone list with the twelve-note list in the recipe. Listen to the different spacing between adjacent keys.",
									"Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @scale   ·   entry 517\nVALUES: atom list; note count followed by cents or ratios\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)\nWHAT: Defines Scala tuning intervals directly as a list.\nREQUIRES: Use pitched notes and pitch tracking. The example has six intervals per octave. Decimal values are cents; ratios use a slash. The 0-cent root is implicit, so omit it from the list. Keep an explicit keyboard map out of this first test.\nTRY: Load the sine example and play successive MIDI keys. Compare the six-note whole-tone list with the twelve-note list in the recipe. Listen to the different spacing between adjacent keys.\nBUILD NOTE: Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.\nSOURCE: https://docs.cycling74.com/reference/sfizz~/"
								]
							},
							{
								"key": 518,
								"value": [
									"sfizz~ @scalename REPLACE_WITH_SCALE_NAME @volume -18",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @scalename   ·   entry 518",
									"VALUES: symbol; available Scala scale name; .scl may be omitted\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)",
									"Selects a tuning from an available Scala scale name.",
									"Replace the placeholder with a scale recognized by your Max installation. An arbitrary mode word is not guaranteed to be a valid filename. Use a pitched source; the inline scale attribute is a useful fallback when no named file is available.",
									"// MAX OBJECT ATTRIBUTE: scalename\n// Create this Max object: sfizz~ @scalename REPLACE_WITH_SCALE_NAME @volume -18\n// MAX message: scalename REPLACE_WITH_SCALE_NAME\n// Independent fallback: scale 6 200.0 400.0 600.0 800.0 1000.0 1200.0\n// Save the SFZ below; load it using read. Max settings above are comments only.\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=0 hikey=127 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-12 ampeg_attack=0.01 ampeg_release=0.25\n",
									"Select two available scales with different intervals. Replay a short run of adjacent keys after each selection. If a name cannot be resolved, verify it in the scale archive or use an inline scale list.",
									"Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @scalename   ·   entry 518\nVALUES: symbol; available Scala scale name; .scl may be omitted\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)\nWHAT: Selects a tuning from an available Scala scale name.\nREQUIRES: Replace the placeholder with a scale recognized by your Max installation. An arbitrary mode word is not guaranteed to be a valid filename. Use a pitched source; the inline scale attribute is a useful fallback when no named file is available.\nTRY: Select two available scales with different intervals. Replay a short run of adjacent keys after each selection. If a name cannot be resolved, verify it in the scale archive or use an inline scale list.\nBUILD NOTE: Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.\nSOURCE: https://docs.cycling74.com/reference/sfizz~/"
								]
							},
							{
								"key": 519,
								"value": [
									"sfizz~ @silent 1 @volume -18",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @silent   ·   entry 519",
									"VALUES: int; 0/1; default 0\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)",
									"Suppresses informational console output.",
									"Open the Max Console and use a valid instrument. This controls informational reporting, not amplifier gain; it is not a mute switch.",
									"// MAX OBJECT ATTRIBUTE: silent\n// Create this Max object: sfizz~ @silent 1 @volume -18\n// MAX messages: silent 0 / silent 1\n// Reload a valid SFZ with readagain to compare informational output.\n// Save the SFZ below; load it using read. Max settings above are comments only.\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=0 hikey=127 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-12 ampeg_attack=0.01 ampeg_release=0.25\n",
									"Compare valid file-loading activity with silent 0 and silent 1 while watching the Console. Audio should not change merely because silent changed.",
									"Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @silent   ·   entry 519\nVALUES: int; 0/1; default 0\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)\nWHAT: Suppresses informational console output.\nREQUIRES: Open the Max Console and use a valid instrument. This controls informational reporting, not amplifier gain; it is not a mute switch.\nTRY: Compare valid file-loading activity with silent 0 and silent 1 while watching the Console. Audio should not change merely because silent changed.\nBUILD NOTE: Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.\nSOURCE: https://docs.cycling74.com/reference/sfizz~/"
								]
							},
							{
								"key": 520,
								"value": [
									"sfizz~ @voices 2 @volume -18",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @voices   ·   entry 520",
									"VALUES: positive int; default 64; upper bound depends on build\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)",
									"Limits simultaneous sounding voices.",
									"Use sustained notes, not one_shot hits. Each triggered region can consume a voice, so one MIDI note can need several voices. Avoid region/group voice limits for this isolated test.",
									"// MAX OBJECT ATTRIBUTE: voices\n// Create this Max object: sfizz~ @voices 2 @volume -18\n// MAX comparison: voices 2 / voices 8\n// Note-ons: midievent 144 60 100; midievent 144 64 100; midievent 144 67 100\n// Note-offs: midievent 128 60 0; midievent 128 64 0; midievent 128 67 0\n// Save the SFZ below; load it using read. Max settings above are comments only.\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=0 hikey=127 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-12 ampeg_attack=0.01 ampeg_release=0.25\n",
									"Hold notes 60 and 64, then add 67 with voices 2. Compare with voices 8: the larger budget allows all three to remain sounding. Send note-offs for all three afterward.",
									"Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @voices   ·   entry 520\nVALUES: positive int; default 64; upper bound depends on build\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)\nWHAT: Limits simultaneous sounding voices.\nREQUIRES: Use sustained notes, not one_shot hits. Each triggered region can consume a voice, so one MIDI note can need several voices. Avoid region/group voice limits for this isolated test.\nTRY: Hold notes 60 and 64, then add 67 with voices 2. Compare with voices 8: the larger budget allows all three to remain sounding. Send note-offs for all three afterward.\nBUILD NOTE: Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.\nSOURCE: https://docs.cycling74.com/reference/sfizz~/"
								]
							},
							{
								"key": 521,
								"value": [
									"sfizz~ @volume -18",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @volume   ·   entry 521",
									"VALUES: float; dB; default 0.\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)",
									"Adjusts the entire object’s output gain.",
									"Load an instrument, enable audio and connect the output to meters/listening. Max volume affects the whole sfizz~ instance; SFZ volume= under a header remains a separate instrument setting.",
									"// MAX OBJECT ATTRIBUTE: volume\n// Create this Max object: sfizz~ @volume -18\n// MAX messages: volume -18. / volume -6.\n// Keep note velocity and the downstream gain unchanged.\n// Save the SFZ below; load it using read. Max settings above are comments only.\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=0 hikey=127 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-12 ampeg_attack=0.01 ampeg_release=0.25\n",
									"Replay the same note at the same velocity, comparing volume -18. with volume -6. Watch the output meter and listen for the level change.",
									"Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @volume   ·   entry 521\nVALUES: float; dB; default 0.\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)\nWHAT: Adjusts the entire object’s output gain.\nREQUIRES: Load an instrument, enable audio and connect the output to meters/listening. Max volume affects the whole sfizz~ instance; SFZ volume= under a header remains a separate instrument setting.\nTRY: Replay the same note at the same velocity, comparing volume -18. with volume -6. Watch the output meter and listen for the level change.\nBUILD NOTE: Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.\nSOURCE: https://docs.cycling74.com/reference/sfizz~/"
								]
							},
							{
								"key": 522,
								"value": [
									"sfizz~ @defaultpathmode 3 @volume -18",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @defaultpathmode   ·   entry 522",
									"VALUES: int; 0–4; alias of pathmode; default 0\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)",
									"Provides the alternate name for pathmode.",
									"Use dictionary sample playback and the same companions as pathmode. Configure one spelling at a time; they address the same setting. Mode 3 needs a saved patch with the sample in its folder.",
									"// MAX OBJECT ATTRIBUTE: defaultpathmode\n// Create this Max object: sfizz~ @defaultpathmode 3 @volume -18\n// MAX inlet message: defaultpathmode 3\n// Use the Dictionaries tab of sfizz~ Help for a valid sample dictionary.\n// The SFZ below is only a baseline playback check.\n// Save the SFZ below; load it using read. Max settings above are comments only.\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_SAMPLE.wav key=60 loop_mode=one_shot\nvolume=-18\n",
									"Repeat the pathmode dictionary test using defaultpathmode 3. It should select the same path policy as pathmode 3; it does not add a second search location.",
									"Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.",
									"sfizz~ Object Attributes / @defaultpathmode   ·   entry 522\nVALUES: int; 0–4; alias of pathmode; default 0\nSCOPE: Max sfizz~ object (outside SFZ headers)\nWHAT: Provides the alternate name for pathmode.\nREQUIRES: Use dictionary sample playback and the same companions as pathmode. Configure one spelling at a time; they address the same setting. Mode 3 needs a saved patch with the sample in its folder.\nTRY: Repeat the pathmode dictionary test using defaultpathmode 3. It should select the same path policy as pathmode 3; it does not add a second search location.\nBUILD NOTE: Cycling ’74 object reference; examples are teaching recipes, not a Max runtime verification.\nSOURCE: https://docs.cycling74.com/reference/sfizz~/"
								]
							}
						]
					},
