									"text": "Counts individual audio channels: @outputs 8 = 4 stereo pairs. SFZ output=p\nselects a pair, starting at 0; the default output=0 uses channels 1/2.\nChannels: 1=L1, 2=R1, 3=L2, 4=R2, …, 1023=L512, 1024=R512.\nSFZ output=p: L channel = 2p+1; R channel = 2p+2.\nUse an even @outputs count for complete pairs; connect the selected channels\nto meters/audio.\nOpen “Output channel map 1–1024” in the main browser for every pair.\nTry: Load this recipe in sfizz~ @outputs 8. Play MIDI 60, 61, 62, then 63: meter\nactivity should move through channels 1/2, 3/4, 5/6, then 7/8. Send note-offs\nbetween notes. @outputs allocates channels; each region’s output= chooses\nits destination.",
